<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yahya ibn Abdallah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 803</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yahya ibn Abdallah was an Alid, a descendant of the Prophet through al-Hasan, who survived the failed Alid revolt at Fakhkh in 786. Around 791 he raised a rebellion in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daylam">Daylam</a> with the support of the local Justanid king, but surrendered to the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid</a> on a promise of safety. He was later imprisoned and died in captivity.</p></div>
